<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yevgeny Alekseyev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1843–1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Yevgeni Alekseyev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yevgeny Alekseyev was a Russian admiral who commanded the Pacific Squadron and governed the Kwantung Oblast from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Port Arthur</a>, and in 1903 was appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> of the Far East. His forceful policy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> helped bring on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a>, in which he was briefly commander-in-chief before being recalled in late 1904. He was widely rumoured to be an illegitimate son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a>.</p></div>
